[2026-03-04T20:20:34.036Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qt3YqyPYPWTUHHST7ZeXKT","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# deploy-verification\n     2→\n     3→## Purpose\n     4→\n     5→Verifies that a deployed app is fully operational after `npm run deploy` completes. Deployment\n     6→alone does not guarantee the app works — the database connection must be configured on Netlify\n     7→and API endpoints must be reachable.\n     8→\n     9→## Post-Deploy Verification Steps\n    10→\n    11→Run these steps in order after a successful `npm run deploy`:\n    12→\n    13→### 1. Set DATABASE_URL on Netlify\n    14→\n    15→The deploy script sets up the database and deploys the app, but does NOT automatically configure\n    16→the `DATABASE_URL` environment variable on the Netlify site. Without it, all backend functions\n    17→will return 500 errors.\n    18→\n    19→Set it using the Netlify REST API (see `skills/scripts/netlify-env.md`):\n    20→\n    21→```bash\n    22→curl -s -X POST \"https://api.netlify.com/api/v1/accounts/${NETLIFY_ACCOUNT_SLUG}/env?site_id=${NETLIFY_SITE_ID}\" \\\n    23→  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN\" \\\n    24→  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n    25→  -d '[{\"key\":\"DATABASE_URL\",\"values\":[{\"value\":\"'\"$DATABASE_URL\"'\",\"context\":\"all\"}]}]'\n    26→```\n    27→\n    28→### 2. Verify API endpoints return 200\n    29→\n    30→Test at least one backend endpoint to confirm the database connection works:\n    31→\n    32→```bash\n    33→curl -s -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code}\" https://<site-url>/.netlify/functions/<function-name>\n    34→```\n    35→\n    36→If this returns 500, the `DATABASE_URL` is likely not set or is incorrect. Do not proceed to\n    37→deployment tests until API endpoints respond successfully.\n    38→\n    39→### 3. Run deployment tests\n    40→\n    41→Only run deployment tests after confirming API endpoints are healthy. Deployment tests that\n    42→hit broken endpoints will produce misleading failures.\n    43→\n    44→**Testing constraints:**\n    45→\n    46→- **No significant side effects**: Deployment tests must not perform actions with significant\n    47→  side effects (e.g., sending emails, triggering external webhooks, deleting critical data).\n    48→  Test read-heavy flows and minor CRUD operations only.\n    49→- **Revert database changes**: Any database changes made during deployment tests (created rows,\n    50→  updated records, etc.) must be reverted after the test finishes. The production database\n    51→  should be left in the same state it was in before testing. Use API DELETE endpoints or direct\n    52→  SQL cleanup to undo changes.\n    53→\n    54→## Common Failures\n    55→\n    56→- **500 from API endpoints**: `DATABASE_URL` not set on Netlify. Set it per step 1.\n    57→- **\"No project id found\" from Netlify CLI**: Use the REST API instead of `npx netlify env:set`.\n    58→  See `skills/scripts/netlify-env.md`.\n    59→- **Deployment tests fail on empty data**: If tests expect seeded data but the production database\n    60→  is empty, seed the production database or adjust tests to handle empty states.\n    61→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"052800dd-b132-492c-9068-83957881166c","uuid":"95f2fd9c-3c12-4a39-b43f-01524682cb38","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/repo/skills/scripts/deploy-verification.md","content":"# deploy-verification\n\n## Purpose\n\nVerifies that a deployed app is fully operational after `npm run deploy` completes. Deployment\nalone does not guarantee the app works — the database connection must be configured on Netlify\nand API endpoints must be reachable.\n\n## Post-Deploy Verification Steps\n\nRun these steps in order after a successful `npm run deploy`:\n\n### 1. Set DATABASE_URL on Netlify\n\nThe deploy script sets up the database and deploys the app, but does NOT automatically configure\nthe `DATABASE_URL` environment variable on the Netlify site. Without it, all backend functions\nwill return 500 errors.\n\nSet it using the Netlify REST API (see `skills/scripts/netlify-env.md`):\n\n```bash\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://api.netlify.com/api/v1/accounts/${NETLIFY_ACCOUNT_SLUG}/env?site_id=${NETLIFY_SITE_ID}\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '[{\"key\":\"DATABASE_URL\",\"values\":[{\"value\":\"'\"$DATABASE_URL\"'\",\"context\":\"all\"}]}]'\n```\n\n### 2. Verify API endpoints return 200\n\nTest at least one backend endpoint to confirm the database connection works:\n\n```bash\ncurl -s -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code}\" https://<site-url>/.netlify/functions/<function-name>\n```\n\nIf this returns 500, the `DATABASE_URL` is likely not set or is incorrect. Do not proceed to\ndeployment tests until API endpoints respond successfully.\n\n### 3. Run deployment tests\n\nOnly run deployment tests after confirming API endpoints are healthy. Deployment tests that\nhit broken endpoints will produce misleading failures.\n\n**Testing constraints:**\n\n- **No significant side effects**: Deployment tests must not perform actions with significant\n  side effects (e.g., sending emails, triggering external webhooks, deleting critical data).\n  Test read-heavy flows and minor CRUD operations only.\n- **Revert database changes**: Any database changes made during deployment tests (created rows,\n  updated records, etc.) must be reverted after the test finishes. The production database\n  should be left in the same state it was in before testing. Use API DELETE endpoints or direct\n  SQL cleanup to undo changes.\n\n## Common Failures\n\n- **500 from API endpoints**: `DATABASE_URL` not set on Netlify. Set it per step 1.\n- **\"No project id found\" from Netlify CLI**: Use the REST API instead of `npx netlify env:set`.\n  See `skills/scripts/netlify-env.md`.\n- **Deployment tests fail on empty data**: If tests expect seeded data but the production database\n  is empty, seed the production database or adjust tests to handle empty states.\n","numLines":61,"startLine":1,"totalLines":61}}}
[2026-03-04T20:20:34.038Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BCuyuMQkfnCLwDCrs2mhtV","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# env-setup\n     2→\n     3→## Purpose\n     4→\n     5→Documents environment prerequisites that must be in place before running app scripts\n     6→(test, deploy, check). Many command failures stem from missing environment variables or\n     7→locale configuration — verify these before running scripts.\n     8→\n     9→## Required Environment Variables\n    10→\n    11→### Container-level (already set in the worker container)\n    12→\n    13→| Variable | Used by |\n    14→|---|---|\n    15→| `NEON_API_KEY` | test, deploy (Neon branch/project management) |\n    16→| `RECORD_REPLAY_API_KEY` | test (Replay recording uploads) |\n    17→| `NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN` | deploy (Netlify CLI authentication) |\n    18→| `NETLIFY_ACCOUNT_SLUG` | deploy (Netlify site creation) |\n    19→\n    20→### App-level (in each app's `.env` file)\n    21→\n    22→| Variable | Used by | How to get |\n    23→|---|---|---|\n    24→| `NEON_PROJECT_ID` | test, deploy | From `deployment.txt` (`neon_project_id`) or created by deploy script |\n    25→| `DATABASE_URL` | test, deploy | From `deployment.txt` (`database_url`) or created by deploy script |\n    26→| `NETLIFY_SITE_ID` | deploy | From `deployment.txt` (`site_id`) or created by deploy script |\n    27→\n    28→### Verifying environment variables\n    29→\n    30→Before running tests or deploy, verify required variables are set:\n    31→\n    32→```bash\n    33→# Container-level\n    34→echo $NEON_API_KEY | head -c 5       # should show first chars\n    35→echo $NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN | head -c 5  # should show first chars\n    36→\n    37→# App-level (from app directory)\n    38→grep NEON_PROJECT_ID .env\n    39→grep DATABASE_URL .env\n    40→```\n    41→\n    42→If `.env` is missing but the app has been deployed before, populate it from `deployment.txt`.\n    43→See `skills/scripts/deploy.md` § \"Populating `.env` for Redeployments\".\n    44→\n    45→## Locale Configuration\n    46→\n    47→The Netlify CLI requires a valid locale. Containers that lack `en_US.UTF-8` will cause\n    48→`netlify deploy` and `netlify sites:create` to fail with locale errors.\n    49→\n    50→**Workaround**: Prefix Netlify CLI commands with `LC_ALL=C`:\n    51→\n    52→```bash\n    53→LC_ALL=C npx netlify deploy --prod ...\n    54→```\n    55→\n    56→See `skills/scripts/deploy.md` § \"Locale Workaround\" for details.\n    57→\n    58→## Node Modules\n    59→\n    60→Before running scripts, verify `node_modules` exists and key dependencies are installed:\n    61→\n    62→```bash\n    63→ls node_modules/@neondatabase/serverless 2>/dev/null || npm install\n    64→```\n    65→\n    66→If `@neondatabase/serverless` is missing, run `npm install` from the app directory. Note that\n    67→direct `npx tsx` invocation may fail on this dependency even when installed — always use\n    68→`npm run` wrappers (see `skills/scripts/test.md`).\n    69→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"052800dd-b132-492c-9068-83957881166c","uuid":"2368b53e-7cec-405d-babe-af4216c165bf","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/repo/skills/scripts/env-setup.md","content":"# env-setup\n\n## Purpose\n\nDocuments environment prerequisites that must be in place before running app scripts\n(test, deploy, check). Many command failures stem from missing environment variables or\nlocale configuration — verify these before running scripts.\n\n## Required Environment Variables\n\n### Container-level (already set in the worker container)\n\n| Variable | Used by |\n|---|---|\n| `NEON_API_KEY` | test, deploy (Neon branch/project management) |\n| `RECORD_REPLAY_API_KEY` | test (Replay recording uploads) |\n| `NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN` | deploy (Netlify CLI authentication) |\n| `NETLIFY_ACCOUNT_SLUG` | deploy (Netlify site creation) |\n\n### App-level (in each app's `.env` file)\n\n| Variable | Used by | How to get |\n|---|---|---|\n| `NEON_PROJECT_ID` | test, deploy | From `deployment.txt` (`neon_project_id`) or created by deploy script |\n| `DATABASE_URL` | test, deploy | From `deployment.txt` (`database_url`) or created by deploy script |\n| `NETLIFY_SITE_ID` | deploy | From `deployment.txt` (`site_id`) or created by deploy script |\n\n### Verifying environment variables\n\nBefore running tests or deploy, verify required variables are set:\n\n```bash\n# Container-level\necho $NEON_API_KEY | head -c 5       # should show first chars\necho $NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN | head -c 5  # should show first chars\n\n# App-level (from app directory)\ngrep NEON_PROJECT_ID .env\ngrep DATABASE_URL .env\n```\n\nIf `.env` is missing but the app has been deployed before, populate it from `deployment.txt`.\nSee `skills/scripts/deploy.md` § \"Populating `.env` for Redeployments\".\n\n## Locale Configuration\n\nThe Netlify CLI requires a valid locale. Containers that lack `en_US.UTF-8` will cause\n`netlify deploy` and `netlify sites:create` to fail with locale errors.\n\n**Workaround**: Prefix Netlify CLI commands with `LC_ALL=C`:\n\n```bash\nLC_ALL=C npx netlify deploy --prod ...\n```\n\nSee `skills/scripts/deploy.md` § \"Locale Workaround\" for details.\n\n## Node Modules\n\nBefore running scripts, verify `node_modules` exists and key dependencies are installed:\n\n```bash\nls node_modules/@neondatabase/serverless 2>/dev/null || npm install\n```\n\nIf `@neondatabase/serverless` is missing, run `npm install` from the app directory. Note that\ndirect `npx tsx` invocation may fail on this dependency even when installed — always use\n`npm run` wrappers (see `skills/scripts/test.md`).\n","numLines":69,"startLine":1,"totalLines":69}}}
