[2026-03-04T20:20:34.477Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KeWvqpd3RRRjJfd3XpULY4","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# netlify-env\n     2→\n     3→## Purpose\n     4→\n     5→Sets environment variables on a Netlify site. The Netlify CLI (`npx netlify env:set`) frequently\n     6→fails with \"No project id found\" errors in monorepo and CI environments. Use the Netlify REST API\n     7→instead.\n     8→\n     9→## Usage\n    10→\n    11→Use `curl` to call the Netlify API directly. This is more reliable than the CLI.\n    12→\n    13→### Set an environment variable\n    14→\n    15→```bash\n    16→curl -s -X POST \"https://api.netlify.com/api/v1/accounts/${NETLIFY_ACCOUNT_SLUG}/env?site_id=${NETLIFY_SITE_ID}\" \\\n    17→  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN\" \\\n    18→  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n    19→  -d '[{\"key\":\"DATABASE_URL\",\"values\":[{\"value\":\"'\"$DATABASE_URL\"'\",\"context\":\"all\"}]}]'\n    20→```\n    21→\n    22→### Update an existing environment variable\n    23→\n    24→```bash\n    25→curl -s -X PATCH \"https://api.netlify.com/api/v1/accounts/${NETLIFY_ACCOUNT_SLUG}/env/DATABASE_URL?site_id=${NETLIFY_SITE_ID}\" \\\n    26→  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN\" \\\n    27→  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n    28→  -d '{\"value\":\"'\"$DATABASE_URL\"'\",\"context\":\"all\"}'\n    29→```\n    30→\n    31→## Required Environment Variables\n    32→\n    33→- `NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN`: API authentication token.\n    34→- `NETLIFY_ACCOUNT_SLUG`: The Netlify account slug (used in the API path).\n    35→- `NETLIFY_SITE_ID`: The site to set the variable on (passed as query parameter).\n    36→\n    37→## Notes\n    38→\n    39→- Do NOT use `npx netlify env:set` or `npx netlify env:get` — these commands fail in contexts\n    40→  where the CLI cannot resolve the project ID (monorepos, missing `.netlify/state.json`).\n    41→- The POST endpoint creates a new variable. If the variable already exists, use PATCH to update it.\n    42→- The `context` field controls which deploy contexts see the variable. Use `\"all\"` for production\n    43→  and preview deploys.\n    44→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"052800dd-b132-492c-9068-83957881166c","uuid":"38734cb1-36d9-4a5e-a0fa-52a4f91588c5","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/repo/skills/scripts/netlify-env.md","content":"# netlify-env\n\n## Purpose\n\nSets environment variables on a Netlify site. The Netlify CLI (`npx netlify env:set`) frequently\nfails with \"No project id found\" errors in monorepo and CI environments. Use the Netlify REST API\ninstead.\n\n## Usage\n\nUse `curl` to call the Netlify API directly. This is more reliable than the CLI.\n\n### Set an environment variable\n\n```bash\ncurl -s -X POST \"https://api.netlify.com/api/v1/accounts/${NETLIFY_ACCOUNT_SLUG}/env?site_id=${NETLIFY_SITE_ID}\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '[{\"key\":\"DATABASE_URL\",\"values\":[{\"value\":\"'\"$DATABASE_URL\"'\",\"context\":\"all\"}]}]'\n```\n\n### Update an existing environment variable\n\n```bash\ncurl -s -X PATCH \"https://api.netlify.com/api/v1/accounts/${NETLIFY_ACCOUNT_SLUG}/env/DATABASE_URL?site_id=${NETLIFY_SITE_ID}\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"value\":\"'\"$DATABASE_URL\"'\",\"context\":\"all\"}'\n```\n\n## Required Environment Variables\n\n- `NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN`: API authentication token.\n- `NETLIFY_ACCOUNT_SLUG`: The Netlify account slug (used in the API path).\n- `NETLIFY_SITE_ID`: The site to set the variable on (passed as query parameter).\n\n## Notes\n\n- Do NOT use `npx netlify env:set` or `npx netlify env:get` — these commands fail in contexts\n  where the CLI cannot resolve the project ID (monorepos, missing `.netlify/state.json`).\n- The POST endpoint creates a new variable. If the variable already exists, use PATCH to update it.\n- The `context` field controls which deploy contexts see the variable. Use `\"all\"` for production\n  and preview deploys.\n","numLines":44,"startLine":1,"totalLines":44}}}
