[2026-03-04T20:20:34.529Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LHyXqKDmBRdD3mRHAvcYFX","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# read-log\n     2→\n     3→## Purpose\n     4→\n     5→Reads raw log files and formats them into a readable conversation showing assistant text,\n     6→tool calls, and results. Raw log files contain JSON events and ANSI escape codes that are\n     7→unreadable without this script.\n     8→\n     9→## Usage\n    10→\n    11→- `package.json` entry: `\"read-log\": ...`\n    12→- **Run from the repo root**: `npm run read-log /path/to/log`\n    13→- Do NOT use the Read tool, cat, head, tail, or grep on raw log files.\n    14→- Do NOT pipe read-log output through grep or other filters.\n    15→\n    16→## Prerequisites\n    17→\n    18→**You must run `npm install` from the repo root before first use.** The read-log script\n    19→depends on npm packages that may not be installed in a fresh environment. If you see a\n    20→module-not-found or missing dependency error, run `npm install` and retry.\n    21→\n    22→## Outputs\n    23→\n    24→- **stdout**: Formatted conversation output showing the full log contents.\n    25→\n    26→## Common Issues\n    27→\n    28→- **Missing dependencies**: If `npm run read-log` fails with a module resolution error,\n    29→  run `npm install` from the repo root first. This is the most common failure mode.\n    30→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"052800dd-b132-492c-9068-83957881166c","uuid":"afdb3bc7-fc61-48ac-8460-bf5b1be777e0","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/repo/skills/scripts/readLog.md","content":"# read-log\n\n## Purpose\n\nReads raw log files and formats them into a readable conversation showing assistant text,\ntool calls, and results. Raw log files contain JSON events and ANSI escape codes that are\nunreadable without this script.\n\n## Usage\n\n- `package.json` entry: `\"read-log\": ...`\n- **Run from the repo root**: `npm run read-log /path/to/log`\n- Do NOT use the Read tool, cat, head, tail, or grep on raw log files.\n- Do NOT pipe read-log output through grep or other filters.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n**You must run `npm install` from the repo root before first use.** The read-log script\ndepends on npm packages that may not be installed in a fresh environment. If you see a\nmodule-not-found or missing dependency error, run `npm install` and retry.\n\n## Outputs\n\n- **stdout**: Formatted conversation output showing the full log contents.\n\n## Common Issues\n\n- **Missing dependencies**: If `npm run read-log` fails with a module resolution error,\n  run `npm install` from the repo root first. This is the most common failure mode.\n","numLines":30,"startLine":1,"totalLines":30}}}
